WEBVTT

00:07.860 --> 00:09.690
Whoa, this looks so good!

00:09.690 --> 00:11.490
Did you draw this, Kuku?

00:11.490 --> 00:12.240
Yeah.

00:12.240 --> 00:13.990
They look so cool!

00:13.990 --> 00:15.360
Nico, your voice is too loud.

00:15.360 --> 00:17.120
Are they from a manga or something?

00:17.320 --> 00:19.870
Yeah, it's called "Uron Mirage."

00:19.870 --> 00:22.120
"Uron Mirage"? Wow!

00:22.120 --> 00:23.290
Nico, your voice.

00:23.290 --> 00:24.580
<i>U.M.?</i>

00:24.580 --> 00:25.920
<i>"Uron Mirage."</i>

00:25.920 --> 00:30.500
<i>A battle fantasy manga about sword-wielding
high school boys who defeat monsters.</i>

00:30.500 --> 00:32.050
I WONDER ABOUT THAT.

00:30.750 --> 00:33.300
<i>It has vague worldbuilding,
cool-sounding dialogue,</i>

00:32.050 --> 00:33.300
NO ONE WOULD UNDERSTAND, ANYWAY.

00:33.300 --> 00:34.950
IT'S NOT BAD, BUT ALSO NOT GOOD.

00:33.300 --> 00:37.220
<i>obscure plot developments,
and an overall poorly defined structure.</i>

00:37.220 --> 00:39.390
<i>It's piqued interest
because of its loose ends.</i>

00:39.390 --> 00:43.100
<i>Additionally, the creator
announced approval for fan fiction.</i>

00:43.100 --> 00:47.060
<i>This has given more fuel to the otaku community,
and it has become the hottest series now.</i>

00:47.480 --> 00:50.980
So this is Utsuro,
and this one is Oboro?

00:50.980 --> 00:52.320
They're so handsome!

00:52.320 --> 00:54.400
I said your voice is too loud!

00:54.740 --> 00:56.030
<i>Utsu x Obo, huh?</i>

00:56.450 --> 00:59.740
Kuku, you're getting better and better
at this, aren't you?

00:59.740 --> 01:03.330
I've been getting into it ever since
I started posting on Chitter.

01:03.620 --> 01:04.540
<i>Chitter?</i>

01:05.210 --> 01:09.210
<i>Hold on a sec. I've already seen
most of the Utsu x Obo fanart on Chitter.</i>

01:09.210 --> 01:10.340
<i>It's my daily routine.</i>

01:10.340 --> 01:13.090
<i>I'll even leave comments
on my favorite fan artist's posts.</i>

01:13.090 --> 01:15.130
How many followers do you have?

01:15.130 --> 01:16.800
Maybe about 10,000 followers?

01:17.260 --> 01:20.800
<i>Wait, what? A popular fan artist?
With thousands of followers?</i>

01:21.140 --> 01:23.810
And this one went pretty viral.

01:24.600 --> 01:27.140
- No way, this is amazing!
- Your voice is too damn loud!

01:24.600 --> 01:28.100
<i>Oh, then I've seen it.
I've probably seen that artwork.</i>

01:27.140 --> 01:29.150
- You really drew this?
- He's so hot!

01:28.100 --> 01:31.570
<i>I've seen every single piece
of viral Utsu x Obo fanart.</i>

01:29.150 --> 01:30.730
So amazing!

01:32.230 --> 01:35.740
<i>If she has 10k followers,
that narrows it down a lot.</i>

01:36.490 --> 01:38.820
<i>Wait, is she...</i>

01:39.320 --> 01:41.660
<i>Is she my current
most favorite fan artist?</i>

01:43.490 --> 01:45.330
<i>It's considered rude to expose an artist.</i>

01:45.960 --> 01:50.290
<i>Otakus on social media
resent having their lives exposed.</i>

01:50.380 --> 01:53.800
<i>I, too, don't want people to know
that I'm actually DengekiMelon.</i>

01:54.130 --> 01:55.880
<i>Any further prying shall be forbidden.</i>

01:55.880 --> 01:58.470
Ms. Makuwa,
why are you just standing there?

01:58.720 --> 02:01.300
It's nothing! I just came here
to grab some paperwork!

02:01.300 --> 02:03.100
Nothing suspicious here!

02:03.100 --> 02:05.270
We weren't thinking anything like that.

02:09.850 --> 02:12.230
You girls hurry on home, okay?

02:12.230 --> 02:13.110
Okay.

02:13.110 --> 02:14.360
Have a nice day!

02:15.860 --> 02:17.240
Oh, Ms. Makuwa.

02:18.570 --> 02:20.110
Bye, Ms. Makuwa.

02:20.110 --> 02:21.620
Yes, have a good day.

02:22.990 --> 02:24.950
<i>She's my favorite fan artist.</i>

02:25.700 --> 02:30.830
<i>Ureshino is
"Haimi@SlightlyOutOfReach."</i>

04:03.010 --> 04:08.470
<b>MY STUDENT IS MY FAVORITE FAN ARTIST</b>

04:11.270 --> 04:12.270
O' God!

04:14.230 --> 04:17.520
<i>Haimi's growth as an artist
has really been awe-inspiring.</i>

04:18.190 --> 04:21.240
<i>As a long-time fan who's followed her
since her single-digit follower days,</i>

04:21.240 --> 04:23.490
<i>I feel something akin to parental pride.</i>

04:23.860 --> 04:27.030
<i>First, it looks like she studied
on how to properly apply highlights.</i>

04:27.030 --> 04:28.950
<i>And not just the vibrancy of the skin tone,</i>

04:28.950 --> 04:32.910
<i>but there's been a big change on how
the artwork just appears brighter throughout.</i>

04:33.120 --> 04:34.670
<i>Maybe she got used
to the thick-line technique,</i>

04:34.670 --> 04:37.290
<i>but since the unnecessary lines
have decreased, she can give attention</i>

04:37.290 --> 04:40.460
<i>to those brawny hands and flushed cheeks
so the finished piece looks livelier than ever.</i>

04:40.460 --> 04:42.420
<i>A wonderful example of how
an artist can move you.</i>

04:42.420 --> 04:45.890
<i>Even the vivid spikiness of Utsuro's hair and facial
expression shows his sensitive characteristics.</i>

04:45.890 --> 04:47.550
<i>Ever since the Recapturing Chaos Arc,
she utilized cooler colors</i>

04:47.550 --> 04:49.050
<i>on his shadow and eyes
to show that underlying sadness.</i>

04:49.050 --> 04:50.680
<i>It's the result of Haimi's
sharp investigative senses and observation.</i>

04:50.680 --> 04:52.310
<i>Oh, I only have gratitude
to look upon such beautiful artwork.</i>

04:52.890 --> 04:54.440
<i>And above all else...</i>

04:54.640 --> 04:56.810
<i>The interpretation
of the characters' relationship.</i>

04:58.230 --> 05:00.650
<i>Utsuro and Oboro met through Kasumi.</i>

05:00.650 --> 05:03.400
<i>They specialized in different things,
so they didn't really interact much.</i>

05:03.400 --> 05:06.570
<i>Their feelings toward Kasumi
seemed more important at the time.</i>

05:06.570 --> 05:10.450
<i>That's when lightning struck for the fanbase
on Chapter 35, the training camp.</i>

05:10.580 --> 05:13.660
<i>Both of them were secretly keeping track
of each other's rank within the school.</i>

05:13.660 --> 05:15.460
<i>The fan base started getting excited.</i>

05:15.460 --> 05:18.420
<i>Mainly because Oboro is a solitary character
who possesses strong abilities.</i>

05:18.420 --> 05:21.090
<i>For someone like that to keep track
of another person's ranking...</i>

05:21.670 --> 05:24.970
<i>How special must Utsuro be to him?</i>

05:25.260 --> 05:29.430
<i>She probably had Chapter 57 in mind
when Oboro accidentally whispered to Sagiri,</i>

05:29.430 --> 05:31.720
<i>"My heart and mind are absent...
But people are still here."</i>

05:31.720 --> 05:33.350
<i>That must be the influence.</i>

05:33.350 --> 05:35.270
<i>For a stoic like Oboro,
he clearly said too much.</i>

05:35.270 --> 05:38.440
<i>If you consider the previous context,
he's obviously talking about Utsuro.</i>

05:38.520 --> 05:41.230
<i>The moment the usually cool-headed Oboro
pours out a single drop of emotion...</i>

05:41.570 --> 05:44.240
<i>It's so... precious.</i>

05:45.110 --> 05:48.820
<i>And then, another wonderful thing
about Haimi...</i>

05:48.990 --> 05:50.950
<i>Oboro's complicated feelings</i>

05:50.950 --> 05:53.830
<i>are expressed through the scarf
that he received from Sagiri.</i>

05:54.250 --> 05:56.790
<i>And that pose where his back is toward us,
but his eyes being on Utsuro</i>

05:56.790 --> 05:59.040
<i>just seems like something that was
intentional or not intentional.</i>

05:59.670 --> 06:02.710
<i>Just by taking one glance at this, you can see
how perfectly their relationship is captured.</i>

06:02.710 --> 06:06.300
<i>I don't think there's any other illustration
out there that captures it like that.</i>

06:06.470 --> 06:10.680
<i>I'm sure a lot of illustrations that were affected
by this one will be posted by early next week.</i>

06:11.220 --> 06:12.760
<i>I can't wait!</i>

06:14.010 --> 06:17.890
<i>Oh, I can live again!
Thank you so much, Kukumi Ureshino!</i>

06:18.190 --> 06:20.190
Did you just call me?

06:20.480 --> 06:21.900
<i>I've turned into Hantengu!</i>

06:23.400 --> 06:24.440
Ms. Makuwa?

06:25.990 --> 06:30.160
<i>O' Goddess! My Goddess hath graced me
with thine presence yonder!</i>

06:32.030 --> 06:34.790
U-Ureshino, did you need me
for something?

06:34.910 --> 06:38.160
Oh, yes. I wrote up the draft
for the Health Newsletter.

06:38.160 --> 06:40.790
Could you please check it
and give permission to make copies?

06:40.790 --> 06:42.590
I added an illustration, so please take a...

06:42.590 --> 06:44.960
Oh no, I could never, I am not worthy.

06:44.960 --> 06:45.920
Ms. Makuwa?

06:46.760 --> 06:50.130
<i>Oh, no! I reverted back to my otaku habits
in the presence of my favorite fan artist!</i>

06:50.130 --> 06:51.550
<i>I cannot let her notice.</i>

06:51.550 --> 06:53.970
<i>I cannot let my Goddess
acknowledge my meager existence!</i>

06:54.220 --> 06:57.430
Oh, great work.
All right, let me see here.

06:57.680 --> 07:00.900
<i>I am a teacher!
Let's just get back to that, and...</i>

06:59.310 --> 07:01.310
I WON'T GO EASY ON YOU!

07:02.190 --> 07:03.360
So precious!

07:04.020 --> 07:05.440
Wh-What is?

07:05.570 --> 07:08.570
Oh, no, it's nothing. Nothing at all.

07:08.570 --> 07:13.280
Let's see, this is drawn really well, huh?

07:13.490 --> 07:16.040
<i>That was close, but I need to hurry
and end this conversation.</i>

07:16.040 --> 07:17.500
<i>If she stays here any longer...</i>

07:17.500 --> 07:20.580
Do you like drawing things like this?

07:20.580 --> 07:24.460
<i>Oh no, my mouth is moving on its own because
I wish to talk to my Goddess about art!</i>

07:24.960 --> 07:28.340
Yes! I love manga so much!
I'm a super-otaku for it!

07:28.670 --> 07:29.970
<i>You'd call yourself that, huh?</i>

07:29.970 --> 07:32.590
So, um, do you like reading manga,
Ms. Makuwa?

07:32.590 --> 07:33.590
Not at all!

07:34.050 --> 07:35.600
I'm not familiar with it at all!

07:35.600 --> 07:36.560
I don't watch any anime,

07:36.560 --> 07:39.890
and I really don't know anything about those,
um, voice... actors? I'm sorry!

07:39.890 --> 07:41.980
B-But Ms. Makuwa...

07:42.310 --> 07:46.020
<i>Okay, so I thought Nakime
had kidnapped me...</i>

07:46.020 --> 07:48.690
You quoted something from a manga.

07:48.690 --> 07:50.860
Oh, well, I guess I read a little bit.

07:50.860 --> 07:52.240
<i>Crap, my otakuness is leaking out!</i>

07:52.360 --> 07:54.200
Oh, these manga books...

07:54.320 --> 07:56.200
Isn't that "Uron Mirage"?

07:56.200 --> 07:58.160
Ohh, yes, I've been borrowing those.

07:58.160 --> 07:59.870
<i>This is starting to hurt.</i>

07:59.870 --> 08:04.000
I really love U.M.!
Which part is your favorite?

08:04.250 --> 08:05.670
Um, well...

08:05.670 --> 08:08.250
I'm not really reading it
so I don't remember,

08:08.250 --> 08:10.970
but the Candidate Exam?
Something like that?

08:10.970 --> 08:13.680
The Candidate Exam Arc?
I love that arc, too!

08:14.010 --> 08:15.340
I don't really remember it, though.

08:15.340 --> 08:19.770
The Candidate Exam Arc is when Oboro
enters the story, so it's a really big deal!

08:19.930 --> 08:22.560
And that's when the story
blah blah characters, blah blah blah.

08:24.480 --> 08:26.860
<i>I feel like I'm looking
at myself and it's so cringey!</i>

08:28.940 --> 08:31.530
I'm so sorry, I got carried away.

08:31.820 --> 08:33.900
I almost forgot about this.

08:34.700 --> 08:39.540
You dropped this U.M. event-limited
merchandise in the classroom.

08:39.540 --> 08:42.830
<i>That's a ticking time bomb
if I ever saw one.</i> <i>You're kidding, right?</i>

08:42.830 --> 08:43.870
That's, um...

08:43.870 --> 08:44.750
Ms. Makuwa!

08:45.250 --> 08:47.590
Why do you hide yourself like that?

08:48.090 --> 08:49.750
I'm not embarrassed about anything.

08:50.300 --> 08:52.340
I realized something
when I started drawing.

08:52.340 --> 08:55.840
That it feels good to expose yourself.

08:56.890 --> 09:00.600
I would like to talk to you more about U.M.!

09:01.350 --> 09:02.390
<i>So bright.</i>

09:10.230 --> 09:11.150
I...

09:11.570 --> 09:13.650
I do, too.

09:15.150 --> 09:17.820
I want to talk to you about it, too.

09:17.820 --> 09:19.530
<i>Yuri Makuwa, defeated.</i>

09:17.820 --> 09:19.530
YURI MAKUWA, DEFEATED

09:19.780 --> 09:22.540
So you're a fan after all!

09:22.560 --> 09:24.540
- You should just say so!
- Yes, I really love it.

09:22.560 --> 09:24.540
<b>URON MIRAGE
WHAT WE KNOW SO FAR

OBORO
UTSURO
SAGIRI
KASUMI</b>

09:24.790 --> 09:27.040
You want to make yourself unnoticeable?

09:27.290 --> 09:28.290
Yes.

09:27.290 --> 09:31.710
<b>MY TUMMY IS TENDER TODAY</b>

09:28.290 --> 09:29.790
I want to become like air,

09:29.790 --> 09:32.050
and disappear into the background
so no one can see me.

09:32.630 --> 09:35.550
If you have such a spell,
I'd like you to cast it on me.

09:35.630 --> 09:36.550
But...

09:36.550 --> 09:39.550
I'm against this.
You're just running away.

09:39.850 --> 09:42.060
Yeah! It's so much more fun to stand out.

09:42.060 --> 09:43.720
Yes. Instead of melting
into the background,

09:43.720 --> 09:46.440
we should help you gain more courage
to stand up for yourself.

09:46.440 --> 09:48.350
Moi, Kan.

09:49.020 --> 09:53.860
New witches become proper witches
by helping those in need.

09:53.860 --> 09:57.570
If that's what he desires, then I'd like
to help him with my magic.

09:59.240 --> 10:03.330
Thank you for bringing this to me.
So in other words...

10:03.620 --> 10:05.500
You need a spell so no one notices you

10:05.500 --> 10:08.540
when you want to get up and
go to the bathroom during class, right?

10:07.120 --> 10:09.210
<b>CLASS 1-3
KOWASHI HARA</b>

10:08.540 --> 10:09.210
Oh, yes.

10:09.630 --> 10:11.000
Are you a little kid?

10:11.000 --> 10:13.550
When you want to go to the bathroom,
just "Bam!" raise your hand and go.

10:13.550 --> 10:15.710
That brash lifestyle isn't me.

10:15.970 --> 10:18.470
And didn't this happen to you guys, too?

10:18.470 --> 10:21.100
BANG BANG

10:18.720 --> 10:21.100
- I got teased just by pooping at school.
<i>- Hey, don't poop!</i>

10:21.510 --> 10:22.720
<i>There he goes! It's Poopman!</i>

10:21.510 --> 10:28.100
HAHA POOPMAN

10:22.720 --> 10:24.220
And I got nicknamed as Poopman.

10:24.220 --> 10:26.310
- Wow, boys are terrible.
- Yeah.

10:26.310 --> 10:28.100
Well, boys are little punks, so...

10:28.190 --> 10:29.650
And so...

10:29.650 --> 10:34.280
That's why you want to find a way to go
to the bathroom without anyone noticing.

10:34.280 --> 10:37.900
I'm telling you, you should use the same
courage that brought you to the witch and…

10:38.570 --> 10:39.490
Witch...

10:39.860 --> 10:41.700
Wait, weren't we...

10:41.700 --> 10:44.240
How were we trying to resolve this?

10:44.410 --> 10:45.450
Huh...

10:45.910 --> 10:46.370
Boo!

10:46.370 --> 10:47.000
Whoa!

10:47.080 --> 10:47.790
Whoa!

10:47.790 --> 10:51.040
Nico! Wait, were you here the whole time?

10:51.040 --> 10:53.420
Of course I was.

10:53.420 --> 10:55.250
Yeah. Wait...

10:56.760 --> 10:57.510
Huh...

10:57.590 --> 10:58.760
Huh...

11:00.970 --> 11:01.840
Boo!

11:02.090 --> 11:04.510
Have you been turning invisible?

11:04.760 --> 11:07.560
I cast a spell
that makes my presence thinner.

11:07.560 --> 11:09.270
I'll cast it on you, too, Hara.

11:09.600 --> 11:11.520
Mobliviate!

11:15.070 --> 11:17.030
Huh? Have I disappeared?

11:17.320 --> 11:19.280
Not one bit.

11:19.280 --> 11:21.280
Your presence is still glaring.

11:21.280 --> 11:22.360
Hara.

11:22.360 --> 11:25.870
Take your pointer fingers and go like this,
and then cross your arms.

11:27.290 --> 11:28.410
Huh...

11:27.290 --> 11:28.830
HUH

11:29.910 --> 11:31.420
- Oh, there you are.
- Hey, it's you.

11:31.420 --> 11:33.080
I understand the system.

11:33.710 --> 11:35.210
And then, fifth period!

11:34.040 --> 11:34.920
AND THEN, FIFTH PERIOD

11:35.380 --> 11:41.050
First, I'll go over the basic structure of an atom.
In the center of the atom...

11:41.220 --> 11:45.300
<i>It's already churning.
Plus there isn't much heavy time.</i>

11:43.840 --> 11:45.550
<b>HEAVY TIME
WHEN YOUR TUMMY IS ACHING</b>

11:45.300 --> 11:47.100
<i>It's instant death pain.</i>

11:45.830 --> 11:47.830
<b>INSTANT DEATH PAIN
THE TYPE OF STOMACH PAIN THAT HAS
A SHORT TIMESPAN FROM
BEGINNING TO EXPLOSION</b>

11:48.140 --> 11:50.980
<i>The countdown for the explosion
has already started.</i>

11:51.230 --> 11:54.310
<i>It's the strong max stomach kind.</i>

11:51.850 --> 11:55.060
STRONG MAX STOMACH
THE WORST KIND OF STOMACH PAIN

11:56.150 --> 11:59.400
For example, the hydrogen atom has one proton,
and the helium atom has two protons.

11:59.400 --> 12:01.820
Electrons orbit around the nucleus of an atom.

12:00.530 --> 12:01.820
<i>Okay, let's do this.</i>

12:02.860 --> 12:04.160
<i>Mobliviate!</i>

12:04.370 --> 12:09.580
There are different rings of orbits,
and each one has a set amount of electrons.

12:09.580 --> 12:13.120
<i>Wait, I don't know how to determine
if my presence has vanished or not.</i>

12:13.120 --> 12:18.460
<i>She said that it's more difficult to notice me,
but it's not like I've become invisible.</i>

12:20.920 --> 12:23.300
Atoms are quite small,
and cannot be seen by the naked eye.

12:25.470 --> 12:27.430
However, atoms will gather together
and form a molecule,

12:27.430 --> 12:30.100
and that is what's comprised
of material as we know it.

12:30.470 --> 12:36.110
Water is a molecule made from
two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.

12:33.560 --> 12:36.110
<i>What am I even doing right now?</i>

12:36.110 --> 12:40.440
Our bodies are a collection of atoms
that came together to form different molecules.

12:38.980 --> 12:41.320
<i>This pose makes it difficult
to open the door.</i>

12:40.440 --> 12:44.780
Atoms also play an important role
for chemical reactions. In chemistry...

12:47.780 --> 12:50.740
<i>I thought I was gonna poop my pants!</i>

12:53.290 --> 12:56.130
<i>Okay, it should be fine now.</i>

12:57.000 --> 12:58.590
<i>Oh no, that's...</i>

12:58.590 --> 13:01.380
<i>the P.E. teacher who's famous
for having animal-sharp senses!</i>

13:01.380 --> 13:03.470
<i>Mr. Yajuro Igari!</i>

13:04.050 --> 13:05.550
Is someone there?

13:06.720 --> 13:09.430
<i>What the hell? I'm under a spell
but he can still detect me?</i>

13:09.430 --> 13:11.520
<i>Your five sense are too wild!</i>

13:11.520 --> 13:12.810
<i>Is this "Alien"?</i>

13:16.730 --> 13:17.770
<i>Morihito!</i>

13:20.610 --> 13:24.360
<i>I'll take care of this.
You go poop!</i>

13:24.360 --> 13:26.280
<i>That's really awesome of you,
but what a pathetic situation!</i>

13:27.110 --> 13:28.280
<i>Thank you!</i>

13:28.530 --> 13:31.540
<i>I will never forget this strange scene
for as along as I live!</i>

13:36.670 --> 13:38.790
<i>Now I can't drop my pants!</i>

13:39.000 --> 13:44.050
<i>Why didn't you notice until now, Kowashi?
Huh? I'm such an idiot!</i>

13:44.130 --> 13:48.800
<i>Once I get out of this pose,
everyone will start to realize that I'm missing.</i>

13:48.800 --> 13:52.390
<i>This might be checkmate.
I'm really at my limit.</i>

13:54.480 --> 13:56.310
<i>Class is over. Now's my chance!</i>

13:56.600 --> 13:58.060
<i>I have to do it now!</i>

13:58.520 --> 13:59.560
<i>Drop spell!</i>

13:59.770 --> 14:00.810
<i>Drop pants!</i>

14:01.860 --> 14:03.360
<i>Drop load!</i>

14:05.110 --> 14:06.950
Dang, I almost fell asleep.

14:06.950 --> 14:08.610
I really gotta piss. Oh?

14:09.070 --> 14:10.370
Someone's pooping.

14:11.030 --> 14:11.990
<i>They're already...</i>

14:12.120 --> 14:15.160
Hey, don't bother him.
We're too old for that.

14:15.160 --> 14:17.750
I wasn't gonna. Sorry, man.

14:17.960 --> 14:20.500
Man, that class though...

14:24.510 --> 14:26.260
GRADE 1 CLASS 3

14:25.510 --> 14:26.260
In the end...

14:26.590 --> 14:28.930
I was the only kid there, huh?

14:28.930 --> 14:31.010
Next time, I'll just raise my hand.

14:32.390 --> 14:34.390
It's way better than sneaking around.

14:34.680 --> 14:38.770
I'm sorry, Wakatsuki, for having you
use your magic on a silly problem.

14:38.770 --> 14:40.520
It's not silly at all.

14:40.730 --> 14:45.860
It was causing you anxiety,
so I'm happy to help in some way.

14:46.190 --> 14:48.900
Thank you, Nico.

14:50.530 --> 14:51.820
Something lit up.

14:52.200 --> 14:53.990
Oh, it's my magic stone.

14:53.990 --> 14:55.240
Magic stone?

14:55.450 --> 14:59.250
Inside my wand is a magic stone
that every witch receives.

14:59.620 --> 15:01.630
New witches' stones are blue.

15:01.630 --> 15:04.300
Once you become a full-fledged witch,
it's supposed to turn white.

15:04.300 --> 15:07.880
Just now, the color changed
a little bit more towards white.

15:08.170 --> 15:10.130
Proof of Nico's growth.

15:10.430 --> 15:13.220
Hara's gratitude helped level you up.

15:13.550 --> 15:18.060
It's because you relied on me
for something, so thank you as well.

15:18.060 --> 15:20.480
I only went to the bathroom, though.

15:20.730 --> 15:26.110
I want to keep listening to everyone's troubles,
and help them with my magic.

15:27.360 --> 15:31.240
<i>At first, I really didn't want her
to use magic all that much.</i>

15:32.490 --> 15:34.830
<i>But I guess it's much better
than sneaking around.</i>

15:43.790 --> 15:48.010
<b>ITEM INTRODUCTION
NICO'S WAND

AT THE HEAD
IS THE EMBLEM OF AN EAGLE

WHEN IT'S USED TO FLY,
 MAGIC ENERGY IS EMITTED
AT THE END, AND THUS BEGAN
THE LEGEND THAT WITCHES
FLY ON BROOMS.</b>

15:48.170 --> 15:53.010
<b>ITEM INTRODUCTION
NICO'S WAND

WHILE FLYING, IT EXTENDS

NORMALLY IT'S FASTENED
TO HER BELT ON A HOLSTER.</b>

15:57.770 --> 16:02.730
CAT SCOUT

16:00.940 --> 16:02.730
Oh, Otogi.

16:03.440 --> 16:04.940
Great timing.

16:04.940 --> 16:06.650
Hello, Mr. Seki.

16:07.730 --> 16:09.610
I wanted to drive the van,

16:09.610 --> 16:12.200
but there's a cat under there,
so I can't really start the engine.

16:12.200 --> 16:13.660
Let me see if I can help.

16:19.290 --> 16:21.330
Sorry to bother your nap time.

16:21.500 --> 16:23.710
Thank you! Your ogre strength is amazing.

16:23.710 --> 16:25.580
Let me know if you need more help.

16:25.580 --> 16:27.290
Wow, so amazing.

16:27.290 --> 16:31.970
Hey Otogi, can you come over to my house?
There's a tree that needs removing.

16:31.970 --> 16:33.930
I'm not a gardener.

16:58.990 --> 17:01.200
<i>Stare.</i>

17:00.330 --> 17:02.040
STARE

17:02.200 --> 17:04.290
<i>So that's Morihito Otogi.</i>

17:04.500 --> 17:07.540
I, Nemu Miyao,
would like to have him as a familiar.

17:07.540 --> 17:08.840
Um...

17:09.340 --> 17:11.260
Are you looking for someone?

17:13.840 --> 17:17.850
<i>A-A man.
Don't scare me like that, sheesh.</i>

17:18.890 --> 17:21.100
"Let me know if you need more help."

17:21.470 --> 17:22.680
The heck is that?

17:22.810 --> 17:25.190
Of course you'd become popular
because people rely on you!

17:25.190 --> 17:29.360
Why are you mad at me?
Or are you still jealous towards ogres?

17:29.650 --> 17:31.230
Scary! Annoying!

17:31.230 --> 17:32.780
I'm not jealous!

17:32.780 --> 17:35.240
It just pisses me off that
they're relying on you and not me.

17:35.240 --> 17:36.860
That's the definition of jealousy!

17:37.110 --> 17:39.120
"I'm not a gardener."

17:39.330 --> 17:40.450
As if!

17:40.450 --> 17:41.370
You, too?

17:41.370 --> 17:44.540
You're too cool! Too awesome!
Of course you'd become popular!

17:44.540 --> 17:46.620
Why are you two upset?

17:46.830 --> 17:50.670
Oh, you know. Moi's the only one
who's helping people, you know.

17:50.920 --> 17:53.710
I also want to help people, too, you know.

17:53.710 --> 17:55.550
But you are helping people.

17:55.930 --> 17:58.890
You let a student with a weak stomach
sneak out to go to the bathroom.

17:59.930 --> 18:02.390
That cat from earlier has been following us.

18:03.350 --> 18:04.390
<i>They noticed.</i>

18:04.390 --> 18:07.140
- They don't have a collar, so might be a stray.
- Come here, kitty cat.

18:07.140 --> 18:09.270
<i>Hey, stop!</i>

18:09.860 --> 18:11.520
<i>Don't touch me, you dumb crow!</i>

18:11.900 --> 18:14.990
Aw, it looks really upset.

18:13.110 --> 18:16.030
<i>I hate being touched
more than anything.</i>

18:16.610 --> 18:19.450
<i>I also do not have business
with a lowly tengu.</i>

18:19.450 --> 18:21.530
<i>Yes, my objective is...</i>

18:23.870 --> 18:25.290
Morihito Otogi.

18:25.790 --> 18:30.960
He's well-known in the industry because
he acquired Ogre Qigong at a young age.

18:31.090 --> 18:35.300
I was shocked to hear that
he became Nico Wakatsuki's familiar.

18:35.710 --> 18:39.390
Because nowadays, "Interested parties
would form a contract with small animals."

18:39.390 --> 18:41.550
In other words,
"small enough to become a pet."

18:40.390 --> 18:43.580
<b>ANIMALS THAT CAN BECOME FAMILIARS
MAKE YOURSELF SHINE
WITH A SAFE AND COMFORTABLE LIFE
WITH A WITCH!</b>

18:41.550 --> 18:45.560
But to take in a whole darn ogre?
What cheat code did she use?

18:43.580 --> 18:45.560
<b>GET PROTECTION FROM AN OGRE
AND LEAD A WONDERFUL LIFE!
-ALREADY CONTRACTED</b>

18:45.890 --> 18:47.430
<i>I'm so jealous.</i>

18:47.850 --> 18:50.860
<i>If that's the case,
I have the right as well.</i>

18:51.400 --> 18:53.320
<i>And so I'm here to scout him.</i>

18:53.940 --> 18:56.570
<i>But I'm too shy to talk to him!</i>

18:56.900 --> 19:00.570
<i>This is just impossible. There's no way
I can speak to a boy my age.</i>

19:00.820 --> 19:03.080
<i>Maybe I should go home.</i>

19:03.410 --> 19:06.330
<i>Oh no, that side of me is coming out.</i>

19:06.330 --> 19:09.040
<i>Because of my self-consciousness,
I get shy and lazy.</i>

19:09.040 --> 19:12.840
<i>It's that one typical trope
that gets washed away in love stories.</i>

19:13.130 --> 19:15.670
<i>Deep down,
I'm just a gloomy person after all.</i>

19:16.420 --> 19:20.550
<i>No, Nemu! You can't fall back now.
I'm going to change starting today!</i>

19:20.550 --> 19:24.430
<i>If I make Morihito Otogi my familiar,
I bet even Mother would approve of me!</i>

19:25.470 --> 19:28.560
<i>Yes, I am a witch
from an elite family, Nemu Miyao.</i>

19:28.560 --> 19:31.560
<i>Only the strongest familiar
would be good enough for me!</i>

19:31.560 --> 19:35.020
This cat sure is noisy with her meowing.

19:35.650 --> 19:37.400
She followed us to our house.

19:37.400 --> 19:38.860
<i>What?</i>

19:43.620 --> 19:46.620
DOOT

19:44.580 --> 19:46.620
<i>Well, here I am.</i>

19:46.990 --> 19:50.210
<i>But I am indeed
getting closer to Morihito Otogi.</i>

19:50.330 --> 19:53.960
Hey Kan, let's open
those blind boxes you got earlier.

19:53.960 --> 19:58.630
Oh, you mean my "March of Progress:
The Evolution of Man" collection?

19:59.590 --> 20:01.430
<i>These two are in the way.</i>

20:02.840 --> 20:05.430
Is this cat really a stray?

20:05.430 --> 20:08.520
Its fur looks really pretty.

20:08.810 --> 20:10.520
<i>Don't touch me!</i>

20:11.940 --> 20:15.270
What's up, Kitty?
Want me to pick you up?

20:15.770 --> 20:17.020
<i>I said, don't touch!</i>

20:24.620 --> 20:25.620
<i>Ba-bump.</i>

20:28.080 --> 20:30.700
<i>I had a "ba-bump" without realizing it.</i>

20:32.290 --> 20:35.500
<i>What's with this hand
that can press me against a wall?</i>

20:34.500 --> 20:35.500
<i>Don't go.</i>

20:36.340 --> 20:40.130
As the cat lover, I'll show you
how to properly touch a cat.

20:40.130 --> 20:42.340
<i>What did he just say?</i>

20:42.340 --> 20:45.050
When you engage with a cat,
you have to be gentle.

20:45.590 --> 20:49.270
Start around the neck area,
where they can't easily groom themselves.

20:49.720 --> 20:51.100
They should get happy.

20:51.480 --> 20:53.310
<i>This is definitely a "ba-bump."</i>

20:54.850 --> 20:56.940
You're right! Kitty's not running away.

20:56.940 --> 21:00.400
Kitty's become a loaf!
Proof that its guard is down.

21:00.400 --> 21:03.360
And then, you slowly pet the back.

21:03.490 --> 21:05.700
Almost like you're asking,
"May I touch you?"

21:06.620 --> 21:07.910
Can I touch you?

21:08.870 --> 21:10.040
<i>Ba-bump.</i>

21:14.420 --> 21:18.420
<i>Huh? It doesn't hurt.
What is this feeling?</i>

21:19.500 --> 21:21.460
<i>I've never felt like this before.</i>

21:21.460 --> 21:24.130
<i>I've hated being touched
by others so much,</i>

21:24.130 --> 21:27.510
<i>but here I am
embraced with a sense of security.</i>

21:27.510 --> 21:29.050
It looks super comfortable.

21:29.050 --> 21:32.180
He's even seducing cats. Cats!

21:32.390 --> 21:34.810
<i>Ba-bump... Ba-bump...</i>

21:35.940 --> 21:39.270
<i>Embraced by an ogre's hand.
By Nemu Miyao.</i>

21:39.940 --> 21:42.070
<i>Carrying in the sweet smell of grass,</i>

21:42.070 --> 21:44.400
<i>the spring wind caresses my body.</i>

21:45.030 --> 21:47.280
<i>I lie cradled in a giant hand.</i>

21:47.570 --> 21:51.200
<i>The pangs of joy well up
from the depths of my body.</i>

21:51.700 --> 21:55.080
<i>Mayhap my DNA is doing a dance.</i>

21:55.500 --> 21:57.370
<i>DNA? Oh, right.</i>

21:58.130 --> 22:00.130
<i>An ogre's ancestor is a tiger!</i>

21:59.400 --> 22:00.130
MEOW

22:00.420 --> 22:01.880
Meow.

22:02.710 --> 22:05.050
<i>Whoa, whoa, whoa,
what am I even doing?</i>

22:05.050 --> 22:08.140
<i>Don't be like, "Meow!"
just because he's petting me all over.</i>

22:08.550 --> 22:12.520
<i>Stop meowing... Meow... Hrm.</i>

22:12.520 --> 22:13.890
<i>Allow me to explain.</i>

22:13.890 --> 22:16.440
<i>Nemu Miyao's shapeshifting magic
works in a way that if you fall asleep,</i>

22:16.440 --> 22:18.270
<i>you'll shift back to your normal self.</i>

22:18.270 --> 22:23.320
<i>Wait a second, if I revert back now,
they'll know that I'm human.</i>

22:23.320 --> 22:25.610
<i>In other words, I'll be known as...</i>

22:26.070 --> 22:28.360
<i>The woman who got pet.</i>

22:28.780 --> 22:32.370
<i>No! I cannot! If I fall asleep, it's over!</i>

22:32.370 --> 22:35.040
<i>But this hand... Oh no...</i>

22:36.120 --> 22:36.960
<i>Ba-bump.</i>

22:37.500 --> 22:40.040
<i>Thump... Thunk.</i>

22:40.460 --> 22:41.540
<i>Tunk.</i>

22:42.210 --> 22:45.550
<i>The Tunguska Event.</i>

22:48.760 --> 22:50.850
A-A human!

22:51.140 --> 22:53.850
<i>I'm done for!</i>

22:54.140 --> 22:56.480
Lookie here! I finally got a human!

22:56.480 --> 22:59.350
- Was this the rare one you were talking about?
- Congrats, Kan!

23:02.520 --> 23:07.190
My "March of Progress: The Evolution of Man"
collection is finally complete!

23:07.190 --> 23:10.660
You did it! After trying about 30 times.

23:10.660 --> 23:14.990
I didn't know what I was gonna do
when I got a sixth neanderthal.

23:11.990 --> 23:14.990
Tiptoe... Tiptoe...

23:14.990 --> 23:18.000
I told you not to waste money
on stuff like this.

23:18.210 --> 23:19.870
Huh? Where's Kitty?

23:20.670 --> 23:22.540
Looks like it went somewhere.

23:22.540 --> 23:25.380
And it was just starting
to get affectionate, too.

23:25.750 --> 23:29.380
That's okay. I feel like we'll see it again soon.

23:34.970 --> 23:38.060
<i>Well, despite having "ba-bumped" today,</i>

23:38.350 --> 23:40.980
<i>I was only here for scouting.</i>

23:40.980 --> 23:43.860
<i>I will definitely visit again very soon.</i>

23:43.860 --> 23:47.900
And then next time I shall make you
my familiar, Morihito Otogi!

23:48.490 --> 23:51.360
<i>No one yet knows about the witch
in the next town over,</i>

23:51.360 --> 23:54.490
<i>but Nemu Miyao's fierce battles
have only just begun!</i>

23:57.620 --> 23:59.330
WITCH WATCH anime
is coming along well, isn't it?

23:59.330 --> 24:01.290
I think utilizing the "complete story
in one episode" type

24:01.290 --> 24:03.830
when there's three stories
in one episode is great.

24:03.830 --> 24:05.340
It's thanks to the skills
of the anime staff.

24:05.340 --> 24:08.460
WITCH WATCH also has voice comics
on their YouTube channel, and it's great!

24:07.440 --> 24:12.030
NEXT EPISODE
UNDER THE LOVERS' TREE

24:08.460 --> 24:09.760
Please check it out if you can!

24:09.760 --> 24:12.030
It's Nico from the voice comics.
